Moral of the story: if your wizard is generated with a ring of conflict 
and a ring of invisibility and finds an altar on lvl 6 where Anhur 
grants him stealth, a lot of chaos can ensue.

That is exactly what my wizard did this game. He was actually very wimpy 
but clever. Instead of engaging the monsters point blank, he let the 
monsters do each other in. The monsters completed ignored me as I sat in 
a corner and watched the fun.

It didn't hurt that there was a ring shop on lvl 3 where I found an 
amulet of life saving. As it turned out, I never needed it, although I 
came close on several occasions. The closest was on lvl 12 or so, when 
an arch lich appeared out of nowhere and began summoning nasties. AC -3 
doesn't do much good vs a minotaur, some trolls and an iron golem. At 
3hp I burned a scroll of teleportation and made for the down stairs.

I did manage to find one bones file, where some obliging archeologist 
left a bag of holding. Nothing important was in the bag (some chain mail 
and a few crude daggers I think) so I uncursed the bag and used it, 
which was good because the amulet of reflection was at the end of Sokoban.

I also got a magic marker with 50 charges at the beginning, which I used 
to write a spellbook of identify when my luck got going. I cast a lot of 
light spells in the mines to improve my divination, so I could ID items 
easily. That makes a big difference.

One odd thing did occur - I could never find anything that gave me fire 
resistance. I didn't want to enter Gehennom without that, so I wound up 
wishing for 2 blessed tins of red dragon meat, as well as some better 
armor and another magic marker and some blessed genocide scrolls (no 
need to end the game prematurely because of a nasty mind flayer).

I managed to get Magicbane, albeit kind of late - I got it up to +7 and 
went on the quest. The dark one obligingly went down without much fight.

After that, the game kind of played itself, although my first encounter 
with Rodney really wasn't ideal. It was like, FoD, you miss...FoD, you 
miss, FoD, you miss...meanwhile, Rodney started populating the level 
with nasties. I finally managed to take him down, but my power went from 
345 to 3 in the process.

The high priest went down quickly, and I only had to kill Rodney 3 
times, which is a record for me...it's usually like 7 or 8 times or 
more. And for the first time in a long while, I found the high altar on 
my first attempt.

